1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,667
<i>“Later” always sounds like a promise.</i>

2
00:00:07,333 --> 00:00:09,733
[phone buzzing]

3
00:00:17,467 --> 00:00:19,933
SAM (texting): Busy. Call you later.

4
00:00:31,533 --> 00:00:33,733
MOM (texting): Okay ♥

5
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:42,333
SAM (thinking): <i>Too late to call now.</i>

6
00:00:42,733 --> 00:00:44,733
SAM (thinking): <i>Tomorrow.</i>

7
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,067
[phone buzzing]

8
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:01,333
SAM: Not now.

9
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:24,867
SAM (to himself): She’d call if it was important.

10
00:01:52,933 --> 00:01:56,333
MOM (voicemail): Hi, sweetheart. Nothing important.

11
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:01,400
MOM (voicemail): I just wanted to hear your voice.

12
00:02:05,933 --> 00:02:09,733
SAM (thinking): <i>Forty-seven days.</i>

13
00:02:11,133 --> 00:02:14,667
[a school bell, a train horn — memories]

14
00:02:24,067 --> 00:02:26,867
SAM (thinking): <i>Maybe twenty more visits.</i>

15
00:02:29,333 --> 00:02:37,333
“Procrastination is the thief of time.”
— Edward Young

16
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,933
[reminder set] SUNDAY 7 PM — CALL MOM
Repeat: every week

17
00:02:44,667 --> 00:02:46,733
[train ticket] City → Home · Sat, Jan 9

18
00:02:48,333 --> 00:02:49,600
[phone buzzing] SUNDAY 7 PM — CALL MOM

19
00:02:49,667 --> 00:02:52,333
TEMPTATION: Call her tomorrow.

20
00:02:52,667 --> 00:02:55,200
TEMPTATION: She’ll understand.

21
00:03:00,667 --> 00:03:02,533
[phone ringing]

22
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,733
MOM: Hello?

23
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,667
SAM: Hi, Mom. It’s me.

24
00:03:07,933 --> 00:03:09,667
MOM: Sam!

25
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,400
SAM: How are you?

26
00:03:12,667 --> 00:03:15,400
MOM: Better now.

27
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:29,200
[Mom’s note] SUN 7PM — SAM ♥

28
00:03:34,333 --> 00:03:42,333
“The days are long,
but the years are short.” — Gretchen Rubin

29
00:03:58,200 --> 00:03:59,867
[knocking]

30
00:04:02,933 --> 00:04:05,333
SAM: Hi, Mom.

31
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:08,067
MOM: You came!

32
00:04:26,667 --> 00:04:32,667
[wind; a train passes far away]

33
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:45,200
<i>No calendar has a day called “Later.”</i>

34
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:55,667
LATER
<i>Call her today.</i>

